Add a fixed-speed print entry point to supvan-proto.

The vendor Windows SDK always sets PrintSet.Speed = 40. The upstream library
picks a speed from the compressed size of each block, which lands on 60 for
sparse pages; at 60 every dot is heated for less time and thin strokes print
faint. This mirrors the SDK.

Apply in the supvan-cups checkout (path: crates/supvan-proto/src/printer.rs).

--- a/crates/supvan-proto/src/printer.rs
+++ b/crates/supvan-proto/src/printer.rs
@@ pub async fn print_buffers(&self, buffers: &[[u8; PRINT_BUF_SIZE]]) -> Result<()> {
         let page = compress_buffers(buffers, self.transport.flow().packing())?;
         self.print_compressed(&page).await
     }
+
+    /// Print buffers at an explicit feed speed.
+    ///
+    /// The vendor Windows SDK sets `PrintSet.Speed = 40` for every job; the
+    /// automatic table in [`crate::speed`] picks 60 for sparse pages, and the
+    /// higher speed burns each dot for less time — thin strokes come out
+    /// faint. Use this to reproduce the SDK's output exactly.
+    pub async fn print_buffers_at_speed(
+        &self,
+        buffers: &[[u8; PRINT_BUF_SIZE]],
+        speed: u16,
+    ) -> Result<()> {
+        let mut page = compress_buffers(buffers, self.transport.flow().packing())?;
+        page.speed = speed;
+        self.print_compressed(&page).await
+    }
